cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Peru crop classifier: land-use classification from satellite imagery
  using legacy land-titling records as labels
message: If you use this software or its findings, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Ash
    email: danielmartinash@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/ash2d/peru-crop-classifier
abstract: >-
  A land-use classifier for Peru built from Landsat and Sentinel-2 imagery,
  labelled with the crop declarations recorded by Peru's PETT/COFOPRI
  land-titling programme (~1997-2006), and used to ask whether farmland has
  shifted from domestic annual crops to export perennial crops and whether
  secure legal title makes that shift more likely.

  Headline findings: the shift is large (+9.9 pp of parcels, +12.5 pp of
  cadastral area, ~1999 to 2012, measured from two declarations with no
  classifier involved); tenure does not appear to cause it (a two-period
  difference-in-differences returns a bounded null of -0.0011
  [-0.0126, +0.0104]); and the single-year classifier reaches 0.774 macro-F1
  on a locked test while four separate attempts to read a per-parcel time
  series out of it failed pre-registered gates.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - crop classification
  - land tenure
  - Peru
  - Sentinel-2
  - Landsat
  - difference-in-differences
license: MIT
